   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2019-09-11",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The Health Insurance Amendment (Bonded Medical Programs) Reform Bill 2019 introduces a statutory Bonded Medical Program from 1 January 2020, consolidating existing schemes under a single legislative framework with $20.2 million in funding, to address doctor shortages in regional, rural and remote Australia by requiring participants to work in underserviced areas in return for a university place."
  },
